From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: reopen a file by name where dup is refused.

This console will not duplicate a descriptor by any means: dup, dup2,
fcntl(F_DUPFD) and sceKernelRdup all fail, for regular files, directories, shm
objects, sockets and pipes alike (src/dup-probe).

A file-backed fd does not need duplicating: reopening orig->unix_name gives
what dup would have, an independent descriptor with its own offset and close.
Report the failure with the name it had, so a run says whether there was a path
to reopen at all.
---
diff --git a/server/fd.c b/server/fd.c
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -2004,8 +2004,37 @@ struct fd *dup_fd_object( struct fd *orig, unsigned int access, unsigned int sha
     {
         struct closed_fd *closed = mem_alloc( sizeof(*closed) );
         if (!closed) goto failed;
-        if ((fd->unix_fd = dup( orig->unix_fd )) == -1)
+        fd->unix_fd = dup( orig->unix_fd );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        /* ⚠ THIS CONSOLE REFUSES TO DUPLICATE A DESCRIPTOR, BY ANY MEANS.
+         * Measured with src/dup-probe: dup, dup2, fcntl(F_DUPFD) and
+         * sceKernelRdup all fail, for regular files, directories, shm objects,
+         * sockets and pipes alike.
+         *
+         * A file-backed fd does not need duplicating: reopening its name gives
+         * what dup would have -- an independent descriptor with its own offset
+         * and its own close -- and shares nothing. A socket or pipe has no name
+         * and still cannot be duplicated. */
+        if (fd->unix_fd == -1 && orig->unix_name)
+        {
+            int flags = (orig->access & FILE_WRITE_DATA) ? O_RDWR : O_RDONLY;
+
+            if ((fd->unix_fd = open( orig->unix_name, flags )) == -1 && flags != O_RDONLY)
+                fd->unix_fd = open( orig->unix_name, O_RDONLY );
+        }
+#endif
+        if (fd->unix_fd == -1)
         {
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+            {
+                extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+                char note[320];
+                snprintf( note, sizeof(note),
+                          "wineserver: dup_fd_object failed, errno %d, unix_name %s\n",
+                          errno, orig->unix_name ? orig->unix_name : "(none -- cannot reopen)" );
+                sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, note );
+            }
+#endif
             file_set_error();
             free( closed );
             goto failed;
-- 
